## Measurement protocol

The local tests/benchmark.py script prepares requests and fresh database paths
outside timing, runs one warmup on its own datadir and seven measured datadirs
per case/variant, rotates variant order, and measures serially. Failed trials
are recorded and halt that run rather than being silently replaced. Deadline
is 15 minutes per repetition. Eight clients have at most 32 requests in flight
apiece, avoiding admission saturation as a throughput confound. Timing includes
client JSON/socket overhead and ends at durable terminal events (evaluate ends
at its response). Startup, shutdown and stopped-writer inspection are excluded.
No observer is loaded during timed trials. Complete RocksDB LOG files are kept;
separate instrumented runs record C-write membership and actual libc fsync/
fdatasync observations. Service sync_write_successes means successful sync=true
C writes, not a physical syscall count.

Overhead is measured first with 4,096 tiny evaluate requests and 64 evaluate
requests containing a valid supplied transaction followed by 256 KiB padding in
prefix mode. Durable and mixed-priority tests use 2,048 tiny jobs. The mixed case
has 3/4 high and 1/4 normal requests, reporting per-priority p99 latency. These
are local surrogates, not the campaign-frozen workloads. The broker supplies one
filesystem: fresh datadirs are available, independent fresh block volumes are
not provisioned here. Results cannot establish campaign performance qualification
or a substrate recommendation. Differences within 10% are operational ties.

